Solar-System Orbit Viewer
===============================================================================

Run the configured native/browser application:

```sh
mech run examples/n-body
```

Serve its SVG visualization:

```sh
mech serve examples/n-body
```

Both commands use the same `mech.mcfg` and `n-body.mec`. The timer host drives
a circular-orbit model, the scene host presents projected planet positions,
and the console host reports phase, angular momentum, and total energy.

This is deliberately not labeled as the numerical n-body integrator. The
configured native runner does not yet register the `state/commit` primitive
needed to retain numerical state between timer turns.
